From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 19:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: mux: defer for unregistered switches

The switch and mux match callbacks check for duplicates before checking
whether class_find_device() found a device.  Since struct device is the
first member of both wrapper structures, converting a NULL device also
produces NULL.  That NULL then matches an unused, zeroed result slot and
the connection is silently skipped instead of returning -EPROBE_DEFER.

This lets a connector consumer bind permanently without a late-probing
switch.  On the AYN Odin 3, PMIC GLINK consequently misses the WCD939x
SBU mux and never routes DisplayPort AUX.

Check the lookup result before duplicate detection and explicitly
initialize the result arrays used by that detection.

Signed-off-by: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/mux.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c b/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c
@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@ static void *typec_switch_match(const struct fwnode_handle *fwnode,
 	 */
 	dev = class_find_device(&typec_mux_class, NULL, fwnode,
 				switch_fwnode_match);
+	if (!dev)
+		return ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER);
 
 	/* Skip duplicates */
 	for (i = 0; i < TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS; i++)
@@ -79,7 +81,7 @@ static void *typec_switch_match(const struct fwnode_handle *fwnode,
  */
 struct typec_switch *fwnode_typec_switch_get(struct fwnode_handle *fwnode)
 {
-	struct typec_switch_dev *sw_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS];
+	struct typec_switch_dev *sw_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS] = { };
 	struct typec_switch *sw;
 	int count;
 	int err;
@@ -292,6 +294,8 @@ static void *typec_mux_match(const struct fwnode_handle *fwnode,
 
 	dev = class_find_device(&typec_mux_class, NULL, fwnode,
 				mux_fwnode_match);
+	if (!dev)
+		return ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER);
 
 	/* Skip duplicates */
 	for (i = 0; i < TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS; i++)
@@ -315,7 +319,7 @@ static void *typec_mux_match(const struct fwnode_handle *fwnode,
  */
 struct typec_mux *fwnode_typec_mux_get(struct fwnode_handle *fwnode)
 {
-	struct typec_mux_dev *mux_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS];
+	struct typec_mux_dev *mux_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS] = { };
 	struct typec_mux *mux;
 	int count;
 	int err;
-- 
